{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993335892791001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"foamy-gem-skip","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"1d21b1d56b606edd2a32bff5491c6bbef33c55e7","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 2220-ee4f-f03f-4771","material: d0336a5a8b41ae9e","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 6","regver: 0dbaa5513314ac56","verified-at-sha:3d8be7fec98b4bb0f7367c26c41caecb1dc9b880","dep 4d55330886a46f7f0eefeebc91e70b44de8ba6c3c558de0a4e8b0bfd186caf1a .github/workflows/optionality.yml","dep ceb15f38e826e3886d5c08e746d928559d9868674f0b9d7bc9949ef66d704141 tests/conftest.py","dep cd19a9d2f4ece40695a82310d19f5e29ee2e7a462d6d54b4409bde311d07b5fe tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py"],"signature":"0cb6e9dd5ad7f1ccb085612a738b3d487f52a147da3e979d827474f5a22daca1","signed_at":1782691994705580000}},"author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":7},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"1ba58031366457c0c0ef0ea0f72d56d20ae8075018e202856ebe27e404cd65e4","event_uuid":"7cea6679-e8ce-485d-8134-b103cd2716fb","position":{"commit_sha":"a237fe14cb7ec3bf57b83d5ad2ba2173f681c135","position":"1785330334240821810-7cea6679-e8ce-485d-8134-b103cd2716fb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6c8dfbfe558ef4e63b94402513af8a3c9b064c1bb5ce5b27e750024546ed2495","event_uuid":"feff1505-d936-44ab-b10c-9bc8bcfb6632","position":{"commit_sha":"cf553a30405bc5a908e27eb474f0a357cea6a840","position":"1785339595022057164-feff1505-d936-44ab-b10c-9bc8bcfb6632"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Iso Tester","body":"Plan-review PASS (0 blocking, advisory). Remediation: the sys.meta_path block-extra fixture will (a) be a yield-fixture that REMOVES its finder on teardown (no global import-state leak across tests / xdist), (b) be opt-in (not autouse), (c) invalidate importlib caches it touches. The ALLOW_MODEL_REQUESTS=False net is guarded by try/except (pydantic_ai absent in the clean-core-wheel lane). No gate-logic duplication; test_parity.py untouched. (Plan-review logged container/step-budget warnings — the known gate-internal defect noted on the epic; verdict still PASS.)","timestamp":1782692106520015001}],"created_at":1782605247146731001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"Close the last ~10% of the E2E config-matrix coverage identified by the audit. The team already has strong infrastructure (a dedicated `.github/workflows/optionality.yml` lean-install lane; both gates tested on/off and LLM-unavailable). This is finishing, not building — and explicitly WITHOUT duplicating gate-logic tests (do NOT touch `test_parity.py`'s intended 3-surface duplication).\n\n## Why\nThree narrow seams remain uncovered; closing them protects client-facing workflows across the optional-dependency / gate-flag matrix.\n\n## What / files (gap -> fix)\n- F1 (Medium): the completion CLOSE gate is proven fail-closed only via the library; not driven over CLI/MCP. Add ~2 parametrized cases to `tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py` (drive `rebar transition … closed` via `_cli.main` and via MCP `call_tool(\"transition_ticket\", …)` with `require_completion_verification_for_close=true` + a monkeypatched FAIL verdict; assert blocked + correct exit code / tool-error envelope). Reuse the existing canned verdict — do NOT re-test gate logic.\n- F2 (Low): the completion fail-closed path is only SIMULATED (monkeypatched `LLMConfigError`), never run with the real `[agents]` extra absent. Include `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py::test_gate_missing_llm_fails_closed` in the `clean-core-wheel` lane's pytest invocation in `.github/workflows/optionality.yml` (CI-yaml only).\n- F3 (Low): add `mcp` and `grounding` to the `optionality.yml` per-extra matrix (currently agents/eval/tracing); add a `rebar-mcp --help` boot check for the mcp entry.\n- OSS-standard hardening (cheap adds): a `tests/conftest.py` `sys.meta_path` fixture to SIMULATE an uninstalled extra (precedent: kopf/linkml) so the degradation path is asserted in-suite, and set `pydantic_ai`'s `models.ALLOW_MODEL_REQUESTS = False` as a CI safety net against accidental live calls.\n\n## Scope\nIn: F1/F2/F3 + the conftest fixture + the no-live-calls net. Out: any new test tier; re-testing gate logic per surface (only the surface wrapper / exit-code mapping needs the extra case).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Completion close gate fail-closed is tested over BOTH CLI and MCP (F1) with correct exit code / error envelope.\n- [ ] `test_gate_missing_llm_fails_closed` runs in the clean-core-wheel lean lane (F2).\n- [ ] `optionality.yml` per-extra matrix includes `mcp` (+ `rebar-mcp --help` boot) and `grounding` (F3).\n- [ ] A conftest fixture can block an extra via `sys.meta_path` and a test asserts the friendly degradation fires.\n- [ ] `models.ALLOW_MODEL_REQUESTS = False` guards the suite against accidental live LLM calls.\n- [ ] No duplication of existing gate-logic tests; `test_parity.py` untouched.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py","reason":"F1 CLI/MCP close-gate cases"},{"path":".github/workflows/optionality.yml","reason":"F2 lean-lane test + F3 mcp/grounding matrix"},{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"meta_path extra-block fixture + ALLOW_MODEL_REQUESTS net"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1","parent_status_uuid":"4083da02-113e-4ca6-ac4c-d484fc0107be","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["audit-2026-06-27","oss-remediation"],"ticket_id":"2220-ee4f-f03f-4771","ticket_type":"story","title":"Close the last 10% of E2E config-matrix tests (F1/F2/F3)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2f6fecaa-d07d-4ed2-ae2a-359a91a689a4","b8aa9391-622b-42b4-ac4f-440d0f78e06f","e0307296-28ee-4c40-ba2d-fc7ec4b0e6ac","3cbafcc2-3bd3-41b3-beab-47391288da65","4083da02-113e-4ca6-ac4c-d484fc0107be","09612bfe-76c8-46fd-9ed7-4602a1b744bb","3d3f4240-1600-4e5c-953d-a116ba57b193","6b6db53c-90f8-4e72-8520-ad0f11baa41d","7cea6679-e8ce-485d-8134-b103cd2716fb","feff1505-d936-44ab-b10c-9bc8bcfb6632"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993335892791001,"uuid":"562453f5-f36b-4905-ae7c-80f7a1439d69"}